Q1. What is the Adapter Design Pattern?
Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

The Adapter Pattern is a
Structural Design Pattern
that allows two incompatible
interfaces to work together.

It converts one interface into
another interface that the
client expects.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why do we need Adapter Pattern?

• Connect incompatible interfaces.
• Integrate third-party libraries.
• Reuse existing code.
• Avoid modifying existing classes.
• Improve compatibility.
• Reduce development effort.

------------------------------------------------------------

When should we use it?

Use Adapter Pattern when

• Two classes cannot communicate
  because their interfaces
  are different.

• Integrating legacy code.

• Integrating third-party APIs.

------------------------------------------------------------

Real-Life Example

Hindi Speaker

↓

Translator (Adapter)

↓

English Speaker

The Translator converts one
language into another,
allowing both people
to communicate.

------------------------------------------------------------

Software Industry Example

Application

↓

PaymentAdapter

↓

Stripe API

The Adapter converts the
application's request into the
format understood by Stripe API.

